// spec: a constexpr variable whose initializer the compiler cannot evaluate (it calls printf, which has no kpp body) is an error, as in C++ ([dcl.constexpr] 10) and design.md "Compile-time evaluation" (a `constexpr` variable is a context that needs its constant), never a variable initialized at run time
// error: constexpr_variable_that_is_no_constant_is_error.kpp:12: error: the constexpr variable described is no constant: a call to printf, a C function, which has no body to run at compile time
extern "C" int printf(const char* format, ...);

int describe(int v)
{
  if (v == 1)
    printf("ran at run time\n");
  return v;
}

constexpr int described = describe(1);

int main()
{
  return described;
}
